Example rules for a different AUV scenario (not this one), in priority order:
```
{"condition": "s = 11 & water_visib >= 4", "action": "med"}
{"condition": "s = 2 & alt = 1", "action": "med"}
{"condition": "s >= 6 & s <= 8 & water_visib < 3", "action": "low"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "low"}
```
Rule 1 picks the search altitude when a search starts (the choice is free there). Rule 2 keeps searching at medium altitude while the AUV is already there. Rule 3 stays low while recovering a thruster in poor visibility, and the last rule is a catch-all default that covers every remaining state.
